{"title":"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 30","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> together can do a job in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> days; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> can do it in four days; and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/0/9a08af77df4a8368d896e9a05d57cfb9a7e36a14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> days. \nThe number of days required for A to do the job alone is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/3/77399b568a9a938837c2268fce7d628c0a41ec90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 12 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 2.8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"371\" height=\"17\" />   \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/1900b71723057339142feef3152cbfe3d588f3c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> of the job per day, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/a/15a421b8519a788db422b9150f43792fd6dc4c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> of the job per day, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab2dc239c4e0eae5c9bb4fa82937f6b76b3a4fe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> of the job per day. These three quantities have unit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fb9bcac9fcb85275a34c422853e179f0c97ab51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\text{job}}{\\text{day}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"28\" height=\"40\" />. Therefore our three conditions give us the three equations:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb4656aa152b9324e402ec655f1cb7d8d9ed5c2f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (2\\text{ days})(r_A+r_B)&amp;=1\\text{ job},\\nonumber\\\\ (4\\text{ days})(r_B+r_C)&amp;=1\\text{ job},\\nonumber\\\\ (2.4\\text{ days})(r_C+r_A)&amp;=1\\text{ job}.\\nonumber \\end{align*}\" width=\"214\" height=\"68\" />\nWe divide the three equations by the required constant so that the coefficients of the variables become 1:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/805ff6fce0d95d98bddcb64f75947903ed2dd2c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} r_A+r_B&amp;=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{\\text{job}}{\\text{day}},\\nonumber\\\\ r_B+r_C&amp;=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot\\frac{\\text{job}}{\\text{day}},\\nonumber\\\\ r_C+r_A&amp;=\\frac{5}{12}\\cdot\\frac{\\text{job}}{\\text{day}}.\\nonumber \\end{align*}\" width=\"153\" height=\"132\" />\nIf we add these three new equations together and divide the result by two, we obtain an equation with left-hand side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64b3e4bc4488d8ba66bce0794f71829c4b9c1f1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_A+r_B+r_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"13\" />, so if we subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/7/db7705ad1d9f1e06f3ee1166dec049a808012de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_B+r_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> (the value of which we know) from both equations, we obtain the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/1900b71723057339142feef3152cbfe3d588f3c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />, which is what we wish to determine anyways. So we add these three equations and divide by two:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84e8dbd5827df45b177ffa8e4325dc8d51a33ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r_A+r_B+r_C=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{5}{12}\\right)\\cdot\\frac{\\text{job}}{\\text{day}}=\\frac{7}{12}\\cdot\\frac{\\text{job}}{\\text{day}}.\\]\" width=\"407\" height=\"43\" />\nHence:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/6/306c9f34c6fd76746d5f08a45975411630c2c109.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} r_A &amp;= (r_A+r_B+r_C)-(r_B+r_C)\\nonumber\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{7}{12}\\cdot\\frac{\\text{job}}{\\text{day}}-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot\\frac{\\text{job}}{\\text{day}}\\nonumber\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{\\text{job}}{\\text{day}}.\\nonumber \\end{align*}\" width=\"255\" height=\"112\" />\nThis shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> does one third of the job per day. Therefore, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> were to do the entire job himself, he would require <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/a/f1a49ee6ad19619363a5ce6088c57cb77e8cf8bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" /> days.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME\" title=\"1954 AHSME\">1954 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1954 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1954\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 31\">Problem 31</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_P